websocket: allocate the per-vhost session list without PROTOCOL_INIT

With libwebsockets 4.4.1 on macOS, LWS_CALLBACK_PROTOCOL_INIT is never
delivered to the notify protocol: a session at loglevel spam shows
reasons 71 (EVENT_WAIT_CANCELLED), 0 (ESTABLISHED), 6 (RECEIVE) and 4
(CLOSED), never 27. The per-vhost storage is only allocated in that
callback, so `vhd` stays NULL, ESTABLISHED never lists the session,
EVENT_WAIT_CANCELLED has nobody to mark writeable, and not one
notification is ever written. Clients connect, subscribe, and hear
nothing forever.

Allocate the storage on the first ESTABLISHED instead. PROTOCOL_INIT,
when it does arrive, still allocates it as before.

--- a/src/websocket.c
+++ b/src/websocket.c
@@ -299,6 +299,14 @@
 
     case LWS_CALLBACK_ESTABLISHED:
       /* add ourselves to the list of live pss held in the vhd */
+#if LWS_LIBRARY_VERSION_MAJOR >= 3
+      /* libwebsockets 4.4 never delivered LWS_CALLBACK_PROTOCOL_INIT to this
+       * protocol (observed on macOS, 2026-09-03), so the per-vhost storage
+       * was never allocated, no session was ever listed, and no notification
+       * was ever written. Allocate it on first use instead. */
+      if (!vhd)
+        vhd = lws_protocol_vh_priv_zalloc(lws_get_vhost(wsi), lws_get_protocol(wsi), sizeof(struct per_vhost_data));
+#endif
       if (vhd)
       {
 #if LWS_LIBRARY_VERSION_MAJOR >= 3
